course: dictionary
lesson: 13023
title: Joking or meaning it?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone speaks, not just what they say. Facetiously is one of them. Read the clues around it. «"Maybe the dog did my homework," he said facetiously.» The dog did not do his homework, so Ben is not being serious. He is joking, and he is being silly while others are serious.
explain: Facetiously is often used when someone jokes at the wrong time, such as in the middle of a serious talk. A teacher might say, «Don't answer facetiously», which means "please answer properly, not as a joke". Ask yourself: is this person really meaning it? If not, facetiously may be the word you need.
fact: Facetiously is an adverb, so it tells you how something is said or done.
fact: «Facetiously» means in a joking way, especially about a serious matter, when it is not the right time for jokes.
fact: It can also mean not meant seriously.
fact: When you read it, swap in "in a joking way" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «"Maybe the dog did my homework," he said facetiously.» How was Ben speaking? | Seriously, and he meant every word | *In a joking way | Angrily and loudly | Sadly, with tears
exercise: Sam answered the teacher's serious question facetiously. What does this tell you? | He answered in a whisper | He answered carefully and truthfully | *He answered as a joke, not seriously | He did not answer at all
exercise: «"Sure, I'll fly to school," Ana said facetiously.» Is Ana being serious? | No, she is asleep | *No, she is joking | Yes, she is planning to fly | Yes, she is very angry
test: «"The bell is broken again, so we'll stay at school forever," Rory said facetiously.» Is Rory serious? | *No, he is joking | Yes, he is crying | No, he is reading | Yes, he means every word
test: Which phrase is the best swap for facetiously in «He said facetiously that he was the king of the school»? | Angrily and loudly | *In a joking way | Sadly and slowly | Very quietly
exam: «"Yes, I'd love to do maths on a Sunday," Lily said facetiously, rolling her eyes.» What does facetiously tell you? | She is falling asleep | *She is joking and does not mean it | She is excited and really means it | She is about to cry
